 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A queue belongs to one entity and has:
+
+- `name`.
+- `slug`, unique within the entity.
+- `is_active` flag (default true).
+- Optional `labels_i18n` (JSON).
+
 ### Ticket
 
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `called_at` and `called_by` (filled when called). Attributes:
@@ -75,6 +84,12 @@ ### Ticket
 - Priority (numeric, see below).
 - Issuance timestamp (ordering "oldest first" within same priority).
 - Issuance channel: totem, virtual, printed copy, etc.
+- Display `code`: per-queue sequence `A001`, `A002`, ... (prefix `A`, at least 3 digits, zero padded; beyond 999 it grows). Unique per `(queue_id, code)`.
+- `status`: `waiting` or `called` (no cancelled status).
+- Call fields: `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (nullable FK to users), filled on call.
+- Issuance rejects inactive queues; negative priority is rejected.
+- After issuance all fields are immutable except `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`).
+- A ticket can be called exactly once; only members of the ticket's entity may call.
 
